---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getPublishedBakeries } from '../lib/bakery';
const bakeries = await getPublishedBakeries();
---
<Base
  title="About Detroit Bakery"
  description="Who runs this guide, what it is for, how it makes money, and what it deliberately does not do."
>
  <section class="wrap narrow">
    <h1>About this guide</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Detroit Bakery is an independent guide to bakeries in Detroit and the cities around
      it. It exists because the useful facts about a bakery, the ones that decide whether
      you can actually buy what you need, are scattered, unpublished, or out of date
      everywhere else.
    </p>

    <h2>What it tries to do</h2>
    <p>
      Answer the specific questions a listing site does not. How far ahead do I have to
      order a cake. Who is open on Sunday. Who sells paczki in August. What does the
      bakery itself say about vegan options. We keep a deliberately small number of
      listings, currently {bakeries.length}, and re-check them, rather than publishing
      hundreds we cannot maintain.
    </p>

    <h2>What it is not</h2>
    <p>
      It is not a review site, and we do not rank bakeries by quality. We have not eaten
      at all of these places and we are not going to pretend otherwise. It is not
      affiliated with any bakery, and a listing is not an endorsement. It is not a lead
      broker: we do not collect your details and sell them on.
    </p>

    <h2>How it makes money</h2>
    <p>
      Right now, it does not. If that changes it will be through clearly labelled sponsored
      placement, sold to bakeries, shown in its own area and never mixed into the ordinary
      listings. Paying will never buy a better position in the standard list, a change to
      the facts, or removal of anything accurate. Free listings stay free.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      If something here is wrong, please
      <a href="/update-listing/">tell us</a>. Corrections from a bakery about its own
      details get priority and we aim to fix them within a week. We would rather be
      corrected than be wrong.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
